#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do I cite Qiskit in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-qiskit-in-my-research}"
msgstr "Paano ko isi-cite ang Qiskit sa aking pananaliksik? {#how-do-i-cite-qiskit-in-my-research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cite Qiskit by using the included [BibTeX file](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CITATION.bib).\n"
msgstr "I-cite ang Qiskit gamit ang kasamang [BibTeX file](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CITATION.bib).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do I cite an IBM Quantum computer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-an-ibm-quantum-computer-in-my-research}"
msgstr "Paano ko isi-cite ang isang IBM Quantum computer sa aking pananaliksik? {#how-do-i-cite-an-ibm-quantum-computer-in-my-research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For research papers, we encourage authors to acknowledge IBM Quantum&reg; by using:\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga research paper, hinihikayat namin ang mga may-akda na kilalanin ang IBM Quantum&reg; sa pamamagitan ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ">    We acknowledge the use of IBM Quantum services for this work. The views expressed are those of the authors, and do not reflect the official policy or position of IBM or the IBM Quantum team.\n"
msgstr ">    We acknowledge the use of IBM Quantum services for this work. The views expressed are those of the authors, and do not reflect the official policy or position of IBM or the IBM Quantum team.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paper references should use the following citation:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sanggunian sa papel ay dapat gumamit ng sumusunod na citation:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> IBM Quantum. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/, YYYY\n"
msgstr "> IBM Quantum. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/, YYYY\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum processing units in the paper should be referenced by their unique name (for example, `ibmq_vigo`) and optionally\n"
"adding the version (for example, `ibmq_vigo` v1.0.2).  We also encourage referencing the processor.\n"
"For example:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum processing unit sa papel ay dapat i-reference gamit ang kanilang natatanging pangalan (halimbawa, `ibmq_vigo`) at maaaring idagdag ang bersyon (halimbawa, `ibmq_vigo` v1.0.2). Hinihikayat din naming i-reference ang processor.\n"
"Halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> In this paper we used `ibmq_vigo`, which is one of the IBM Quantum Canary processors.\n"
msgstr "> In this paper we used `ibmq_vigo`, which is one of the IBM Quantum Canary processors.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example of citing an IBM Quantum program:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng pag-cite ng IBM Quantum program:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> IBM Quantum (2025). Estimator primitive (Version x.y.z) [computer software]. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/\n"
msgstr "> IBM Quantum (2025). Estimator primitive (Version x.y.z) [computer software]. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do I cite IBM Quantum Composer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-ibm-quantum-composer-in-my-research}"
msgstr "Paano ko isi-cite ang IBM Quantum Composer sa aking pananaliksik? {#how-do-i-cite-ibm-quantum-composer-in-my-research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example citation for IBM Quantum Composer:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng citation para sa IBM Quantum Composer:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> IBM Quantum Composer. 2025. url: https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer</span>\n"
msgstr "> IBM Quantum Composer. 2025. url: https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer</span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "I don't see something in the user interface, such as my administration tasks. {#i-dont-see-something-in-the-user-interface-such-as-my-administration-tasks}"
msgstr "Hindi ko nakikita ang isang bagay sa user interface, tulad ng mga gawain sa administrasyon. {#i-dont-see-something-in-the-user-interface-such-as-my-administration-tasks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Try choosing a different account from the account switcher in the header of the [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) interface.\n"
msgstr "Subukang pumili ng ibang account mula sa account switcher sa header ng [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) na interface.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "I'm just using the Open Plan, but I had to put in my credit card.  Will I be charged? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-will-i-be-charged}"
msgstr "Gumagamit lang ako ng Open Plan, pero naglagay pa rin ako ng credit card. Sisisingilin ba ako? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-will-i-be-charged}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You will not be charged unless you create a Pay-As-You-Go [instance](/guides/instances) and use it to send workloads to QPUs. See [Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) for instructions to set a cost limit and to learn about other ways to manage costs.\n"
msgstr "Hindi ka sisisingilin maliban kung gumawa ka ng Pay-As-You-Go [instance](/guides/instances) at ginamitin ito para magpadala ng mga workload sa QPUs. Tingnan ang [Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) para sa mga tagubilin sa pagtatakda ng limitasyon sa gastos at para malaman ang iba pang paraan ng pamamahala ng gastos.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What's the difference between an API key and an API token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"
msgstr "Ano ang pagkakaiba ng API key at API token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There's no difference.  The terms API key and API token are used interchangeably. You'll see both terms in the documentation because different interfaces use different terms.\n"
msgstr "Wala itong pagkakaiba. Ang mga terminong API key at API token ay ginagamit nang palitan. Makikita mo ang parehong termino sa dokumentasyon dahil gumagamit ng iba't ibang termino ang iba't ibang interface.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What's the difference between an API token and a bearer token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr "Ano ang pagkakaiba ng API token at bearer token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An API token is a long-lived credential used to [authenticate to IBM Quantum Compute Service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate).  A bearer token is a temporary credential that is used to [authenticate to the REST API in an untrusted environment](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment).  A bearer token cannot be used to authenticate to IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "Ang API token ay isang pangmatagalang kredensyal na ginagamit para [mag-authenticate sa IBM Quantum Compute Service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate).  Ang bearer token ay isang pansamantalang kredensyal na ginagamit para [mag-authenticate sa REST API sa hindi pinagkakatiwalaang kapaligiran](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment).  Ang bearer token ay hindi maaaring gamitin para mag-authenticate sa IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do I have to choose the region that I live in? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-region-that-i-live-in}"
msgstr "Kailangan ko bang pumili ng rehiyon na tinitirhan ko? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-region-that-i-live-in}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "No. You can use either region.  The region determines where jobs are run and where the data is kept.  Additionally, you can only see and use instances that were created in the instance that you are logged in to. Note that only the us-east region supports the Open Plan.\n"
msgstr "Hindi. Maaari kang gumamit ng alinmang rehiyon. Tinutukoy ng rehiyon kung saan pinapatakbo ang mga trabaho at kung saan pinapanatili ang data. Bukod dito, makikita at magagamit mo lang ang mga instance na nilikha sa instance na naka-log in ka. Tandaan na ang us-east na rehiyon lang ang sumusuporta sa Open Plan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can I connect through a proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-server}"
msgstr "Maaari ba akong kumonekta sa pamamagitan ng proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-server}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, but you must use `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.44.0 or later.\n"
msgstr "Oo, ngunit kailangan mong gumamit ng `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.44.0 o mas bago.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is the data retention policy? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"
msgstr "Ano ang patakaran sa pagpapanatili ng data? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM retains your (undeleted) job and usage data for three years while you continue to use IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "Pinapanatili ng IBM ang iyong (hindi pa tinanggal na) data ng trabaho at paggamit sa loob ng tatlong taon habang patuloy mong ginagamit ang IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happened to Python distributions such as Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, and Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"
msgstr "Ano ang nangyari sa mga Python distribution tulad ng Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, at Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, the command `pip install qiskit` will **only** install the [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). This means that some modules that you have used in the past, such as `qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`, now have to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr "Mula nang ilabas ang Qiskit SDK v1.0, ang command na `pip install qiskit` ay mag-i-install **lamang** ng [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). Ibig sabihin, ang ilang module na ginamit mo noon, tulad ng `qiskit-aer` o `qiskit-nature`, ay kailangan nang i-install nang hiwalay.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr "Bago ilabas ang Qiskit SDK v1.0, ang Qiskit ay binubuo ng maraming iba't ibang Python distribution, tulad ng `qiskit-terra`, ang compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, ang high-performance simulator; ang orihinal na IBM Quantum&reg; provider; at ilang ngayon ay lipas na (obsolete) na package na nagbibigay ng mga partikular na eksperimental na algorithmic o experiment-running na feature.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These separate software packages were combined into what was called the Qiskit *metapackage*, which allowed users to install all of these components together through `pip install qiskit`. This metapackage architecture was removed with the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, and now each of the individual software distributions needs to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga hiwalay na software package na ito ay pinagsama sa tinatawag na Qiskit *metapackage*, na nagpahintulot sa mga user na i-install ang lahat ng component na ito nang sabay-sabay sa pamamagitan ng `pip install qiskit`. Ang metapackage architecture na ito ay tinanggal nang ilabas ang Qiskit SDK v1.0, at ngayon ay kailangang i-install nang hiwalay ang bawat isa sa mga indibidwal na software distribution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of packages to suit your needs. You can also read the [v1.0 migration guide](/guides/metapackage-migration) for more information about this change.\n"
msgstr "Kung gusto mong i-install ang mga package na dati ay kasama sa Qiskit metapackage, bisitahin ang [Qiskit ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) para makahanap ng iba't ibang package na angkop sa iyong pangangailangan. Maaari mo ring basahin ang [v1.0 migration guide](/guides/metapackage-migration) para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa pagbabagong ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do I close my IBM Cloud account? {#how-do-i-close-my-ibm-cloud-account}"
msgstr "Paano ko isasara ang aking IBM Cloud account? {#how-do-i-close-my-ibm-cloud-account}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find instructions on the [Closing an account](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-account-close) page.\n"
msgstr "Hanapin ang mga tagubilin sa pahina ng [Closing an account](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-account-close).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why do I see a message that my account is inactive when I try to log on? {#why-do-i-see-a-message-that-my-account-is-inactive-when-i-try-to-log-on}"
msgstr "Bakit nakakakita ako ng mensahe na hindi aktibo ang aking account kapag sinusubukan kong mag-log on? {#why-do-i-see-a-message-that-my-account-is-inactive-when-i-try-to-log-on}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you see the message \"This account is inactive\", visit the [IBM Cloud documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-ts_accnt_inactive) to learn why and how to fix it, or access [IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com) to verify whether you have any pending actions to complete in your account.\n"
msgstr "Kung nakita mo ang mensaheng \"This account is inactive\", bisitahin ang [IBM Cloud documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-ts_accnt_inactive) para malaman kung bakit at kung paano ito ayusin, o i-access ang [IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com) para i-verify kung mayroon kang mga nakabinbing aksyon na kailangang kumpletuhin sa iyong account.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is the impact of device drift? {#what-is-the-impact-of-device-drift}"
msgstr "Ano ang epekto ng device drift? {#what-is-the-impact-of-device-drift}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The impact of device drift (hardware performance that degrades over time) depends on many factors, such as when calibrations were last run, the specific experiment performed, any TLS activities, and so on. If a particular workload is very sensitive to device parameters' error values, you can perform a real-time device parameter benchmarking by following [this tutorial](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) in IBM Quantum Learning.\n"
msgstr "Ang epekto ng device drift (pagkasira ng performance ng hardware sa paglipas ng panahon) ay nakasalalay sa maraming salik, tulad ng kailan huling pinatakbo ang mga calibration, ang partikular na eksperimentong isinasagawa, anumang TLS na aktibidad, at iba pa. Kung ang isang partikular na workload ay lubhang sensitibo sa mga error value ng mga parameter ng device, maaari kang magsagawa ng real-time na device parameter benchmarking sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa [tutorial na ito](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) sa IBM Quantum Learning.\n"
